    "narrative": "With the league championship stretch run in full effect, Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a heavily restricted outlook as many core pieces are inactive. The sole active play in our lineup is **Brice Turang** (49.63), who faces a Jacksonville starter with a respectable 3.62 xERA. While **Brice Turang** sits in the marginal tier, his dual-threat potential\u2014specifically his elite sprint speed\u2014keeps him in the starting slot despite a slightly unfavorable park factor. We are leaning on his historical recency and his spot in the 5-hole to provide steady production in a day where offensive depth is severely compromised by league scheduling.\n\nThe bench remains stagnant, as stalwarts like **Corbin Carroll**, **Jose Caballero**, **Josh Naylor**, and **James Wood** are all unavailable due to scheduled off-days. Had the calendar been kinder, **Corbin Carroll** would have been an immediate lock given the scarcity of stolen bases, which remains our primary focus for closing the gap in 5x5 Roto. Looking ahead, our roster depth\u2014including **Mickey Moniak**, **Trevor Story**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Moises Ballesteros**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Griffin Conine**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Cole Young**\u2014is currently being preserved to manage our remaining game caps. With the Jacksonville starter representing a moderate challenge, we are playing it conservative, betting that a single high-efficiency performance from **Brice Turang** is safer than over-extending our bench in a low-value spot.",
